{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0012064","label":"choanal atresia-hearing loss-cardiac defects-craniofacial dysmorphism syndrome","definition":"Choanal atresia - deafness - cardiac defects - dysmorphism syndrome, also known as Burn-McKeown syndrome, is an extremely rare multiple congenital anomaly syndrome characterized by bilateral choanal atresia associated with a characteristic cranio-facial dysmorphism (hypertelorism with narrow palpebral fissures, coloboma of inferior eyelid with presence of eyelashes medial to the defect, prominent nasal bridge, thin lips, prominent ears), that can be accompanied by hearing loss, unilateral cleft lip, preauricular tags, cardiac septal defects and anomalies of the kidneys. The features of this syndrome overlaps considerably with those of the CHARGE syndrome.","synonyms":["BMKS","Burn-McKeown syndrome","bilateral choanal atresia, cardiac defects, deafness, and dysmorphic appearance","choanal atresia deafness cardiac defects dysmorphism","oculootofacial dysplasia"],"xrefs":["DOID:0080695","GARD:0010041","MEDGEN:325265","MESH:C563682","OMIM:608572","Orphanet:1200","UMLS:C1837822"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":0,"is_group":false,"n_genes":2,"n_phenotypes":36,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_6d432f12edc6","source":"MONDO:0012064","target":"POLR1A","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:1200","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/1200","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed) — RNA polymerase I subunit A"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:1200","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:1200","snippet":"POLR1A is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:1200 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"